WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.200
The Blueprint: how sankettambare.in is built, drawn as six sheets.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:07.000
Six floors, one site: from the page you see to the scripts that build it.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.200
Episode 01, Site plan: Every feature of the site, drawn as a room.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.200
Every feature of the site, drawn as a room: 11 of them, measured live.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.000
Archives: eight collections, 1,877 rows, one table each.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.800
Ask the Archive: plain-language questions, answered with the pages they came from.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.400
The Atlas: the same pages as an illustrated world, in 6 regions.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.200
Admin is staff only. Row-level security in Postgres is the lock.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.400
Episode 02, Section: One feature, traced down through the stack.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.000
A section through the site: the shells under the roof, the scripts in the plant room.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Ask the Archive touches all 6 floors, from the launcher on every page to the nightly index.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.900
The changelog skips the edge entirely: 4 floors, the browser reading Postgres directly.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.100
Episode 03, The Ask circuit: A question, wired end to end.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.100
A question goes in: "Which forts has he trekked?"

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.250
Keyword and meaning search run side by side, then fuse by rank.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.600
The first model is down. The current falls through to the next rung.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:57.100
Only links the archive supplied survive, and the sources stream first.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.300
Episode 04, Unfurl bench: What a shared link turns into.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:04.000
Paste a link anywhere: the edge writes the tags before any JavaScript runs.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.300
26 pages, each with its own committed 1200×630 card. Nothing renders on demand.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:13.000
A browser runs the app instead, and writes the very same tags.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.200
Episode 05, Shell switch: Atlas or Classic, and who decides.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.000
Two shells, one content. Five rules, first match wins, decide which a visitor gets.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.200
Rule 1, ?view= in the URL, sends them to the Atlas.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.400
Rule 3, Reduced motion, sends them to Classic.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:29.000
No rule has an opinion, so DEFAULT_VIEW sends them to Classic.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.200
Episode 06, Tag loom: One vocabulary across every shelf.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.200
One vocabulary for every shelf: 99 tags, 3,732 links.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.800
Life: 472 micro posts, 7 blog posts.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.600
Lift the micro-blog off the loom…

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.400
…and Technology leads: 18 books, 7 blog posts, 6 presentations.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.400
Every drawing is live: sankettambare.in/blueprint
